            "analysis": "The assistant analyzed education level distribution for top 10 and bottom 10 (step 39). For top 10: High School (5), Junior college (3), Technical secondary school (2). That's proportions 50%, 30%, 20%. For bottom 10: Technical secondary school (7), Junior high school (2), Junior college (1). They compared. This matches Path 2.3.A (Proportion analysis). Sub-criterion 2.3.A.1: They analyzed proportion of each education level among top employees. Met. Sub-criterion 2.3.A.2: They analyzed proportions for bottom 10 (as non-top) and compared. Partial credit (0.5/1). Sub-criterion 2.3.A.3: Accuracy: The rubric expects under 'Comprehensive weighted Top 20%' proportions High School and Junior college each 38% (±2%). The assistant's top 10 (which is ~14.7% of 68) gives different proportions (50% High School, 30% Junior college). However, they used integrated ranking, but top 10 is not exactly top 20% (20% would be ~14 employees). Their top 10 may not match the expected proportions. Moreover, they did not compute overall education distribution per rubric table. Therefore, accuracy is not fully met. Partial credit (0.5/1). Total score: 2 points.",
