            "analysis": "The assistant analyzed team distribution for top 10 and bottom 10 (step 39). Top 10: Group 2 (7), Group 3 (2), Group 1 (1). Bottom 10: Group 1 (8), Group 3 (2). This matches Path 3.3.A (Proportion analysis). Sub-criterion 3.3.A.1: They computed proportion of top employees in each group (70% Group 2). Met. Sub-criterion 3.3.A.2: They computed proportion for bottom 10 (as non-top) and compared. Partial credit (0.5/1). Sub-criterion 3.3.A.3: Accuracy: Among all employees, the rubric says 24 in Group 1, 22 in Group 2, 22 in Group 3. The assistant did not compute overall distribution, but from top 10 we see Group 2 dominance. Their conclusion: top employees cluster in Group 2. This aligns with absolute characteristic. However, they did not verify exact overall counts. Partial credit (0.5/1). Total score: 2 points.",
