    "Requirement 3": {
        "Criterion 3.1": {
            "analysis": "The assistant performed a comparative assessment of service quality for priority 1 customers versus the overall baseline. They presented side-by-side metrics for complaint satisfaction, complaint handling speed, ticket satisfaction, ticket resolution duration, and follow-up rate (instead of 'High' urgency share). Their comparison shows differences: priority 1 has lower satisfaction (2.63 vs 3.00), faster ticket resolution (32.85 vs 37.04), longer complaint handling (40.89 vs 36.80), higher follow-up rate (70.4% vs 50.0%), and higher complaint rate (66.7% vs ~147%). This does not match Path 3.1.A (which expects identical values) because the assistant's data reveals significant differences. However, the assistant's approach aligns more with Path 3.1.B (relative difference comparison) as they discussed differences qualitatively and quantitatively, though they did not compute relative differences as percentages. They concluded that there is a trade-off between speed and quality, indicating that prioritization did not yield experience gains. Thus, the best match is Path 3.1.B, but we must assess sub-criteria.",
