{
    "Readability": {
        "analysis": "The candidate report excels in readability across all sub-dimensions compared to the baseline. It uses clean formatting with clear headings, logical flow (methodology → findings → thresholds → recommendations → limitations), and emphasizes key takeaways through bolding and summary tables. The baseline report, while organized, is more concise but lacks methodological transparency and structured justification. The candidate's visual descriptions (though images aren't shown) are contextually explained, aiding narrative flow. The baseline's flow is simpler but less informative. On conciseness, the candidate is longer but purposefully so—adding necessary detail without redundancy—whereas the baseline is perhaps too brief, omitting key methodological details. Overall, the candidate is more professional and comprehensive in presentation.",
